---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="Contribute" description="How to propose, research, write, review, or correct an entry in The Fisher Index." pagefind>
  <article class="page-shell narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Curated open source</p>
    <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">Help make the index more complete.</h1>
    <p class="lede">The easiest valuable contribution is often not a new article. A stronger source, corrected attribution, clearer example, or accessibility improvement can materially improve the record.</p>

    <h2>Before writing</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Search the index and open issues for the concept and its aliases.</li>
      <li>Open a “new contribution” issue with the proposed scope and primary sources.</li>
      <li>Wait for scope confirmation before drafting a long article.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What a reviewed entry needs</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The standard eight-section learning sequence used throughout the site.</li>
      <li>A precise attribution label and named collaborators or predecessors.</li>
      <li>At least one primary source where available and one modern scholarly source.</li>
      <li>A worked example whose arithmetic, code, or reasoning can be checked.</li>
      <li>Explicit assumptions, current use, limitations, and disputed interpretations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Licensing</h2>
    <p>By contributing code, you agree to the repository’s MIT license. By contributing prose, diagrams, or examples, you agree to CC BY 4.0 and confirm that you have the right to submit the material.</p>

    <h2>Start here</h2>
    <p><a class="button" href={`${site.repository}/issues/new/choose`}>Open a contribution or correction issue</a> <a class="button secondary" href={`${site.repository}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>Read the contributor guide</a></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
